{"id": "2026-10-26-sports-wawrinka-s-last-tournament-starts-in-basel", "date": "2026-10-26", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Wawrinka's last tournament starts in Basel", "summary": "Stan Wawrinka, 41, plays his last career tournament at the Swiss Indoors in Basel, opening against Jiri Lehecka on Tuesday 27 October.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/sport/tennis/atp-tour/auslosung-swiss-indoors-happiges-los-fuer-wawrinka-djokovic-gegen-humbert", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "Stan Wawrinka, 41, three-time Grand Slam champion and a former world No. 3, ends a 25-year career at his home-country tournament. The draw gave him the hardest opener available: Jiri Lehecka of the Czech Republic (ATP 20), who reached the Miami Masters final and the Tokyo final this year, losing the latter to Carlos Alcaraz. They have never met. Wawrinka is ranked 140th and will play what SRF counts as his 985th singles match on tour; a tribute ceremony is planned for Monday 26 October, the evening before. Novak Djokovic, 39, returns to Basel after 15 years on a wildcard (a tournament-granted entry) fresh from winning Beijing, and the other Swiss wildcards face tough draws too: Jérôme Kym against Arthur Rinderknech (ATP 61), Dominic Stricker against Casper Ruud (ATP 24). The tournament's own site confirms Rémy Bertola and Mika Brunold came through qualifying into the main draw", "why": "a 41-year-old ranked 140th faces a top-20 opponent in his final match, so Tuesday could be a short farewell; the ceremony on Monday is the guaranteed part.", "thread_id": "2026-10-26-sports-wawrinka-s-last-tournament-starts-in-basel", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-26", "event_date": "2026-10-27", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Stan Wawrinka", "Swiss Indoors Basel", "Jiri Lehecka", "Novak Djokovic"]}
{"id": "2026-10-26-sports-antonelli-wins-austin-title-waits", "date": "2026-10-26", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Antonelli wins Austin, title waits", "summary": "Kimi Antonelli won the US Grand Prix but Russell and Hamilton scored just enough to keep the title mathematically open until Mexico.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/sport/motorsport/formel-1/grosser-preis-der-usa-antonelli-siegt-in-austin-doch-die-wm-entscheidung-ist-vertagt", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Kimi Antonelli, 20, won from pole by 13 seconds for his ninth victory of the season, with Charles Leclerc second and Max Verstappen third. He could not be crowned because Mercedes team-mate George Russell (eighth) and Lewis Hamilton (Ferrari, fourth) scored just enough to stay mathematically alive: Antonelli has 365 points, 123 ahead of Russell and 124 ahead of Hamilton, with five rounds and 125 points left. Verstappen, Leclerc and Lando Norris (fifth) are now out of title contention (Autosport, 25 Oct). He can clinch at next weekend's Mexico Grand Prix; Autosport's calculation says that because he leads in wins, Russell would need to win and Antonelli finish no higher than tenth, with Hamilton needing the same. At Baku four weeks ago his lead was 66 points. Audi scored nothing (Hülkenberg 11th, Bortoleto 13th). Autosport notes the Qatar and Abu Dhabi races are assumed to go ahead \"amid the conflict\".", "why": "barring a collapse, F1 gets its youngest world champion in Mexico.", "thread_id": "2026-10-26-sports-antonelli-wins-austin-title-waits", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-26", "event_date": "2026-10-25", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Kimi Antonelli", "George Russell", "Lewis Hamilton", "Mercedes"]}
{"id": "2026-10-26-sports-lugano-lead-basel-stall-at-0-0", "date": "2026-10-26", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Lugano lead; Basel stall at 0-0", "summary": "Lugano beat Thun to lead the Super League while Basel, held 0-0 by GC, are seventh.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/sport/fussball/super-league/remis-im-st-jakob-park-gc-holt-sich-mit-kampf-und-zwei-goalies-ein-0-0-in-basel", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Lugano, who also won at Thun on Sunday, top the 12-team table on 31 points from 11 games (ten wins, one draw), six clear of Young Boys on 25 (BBC table, updated 25 Oct) (table). Basel, drew 0-0 at home with Grasshoppers after three straight defeats (SRF); they sit seventh on 14 points — currently in the bottom-half \"relegation round\" slot, a split that happens after 33 games and sets who plays for the title. Basel travel to leaders Lugano next Sunday, 1 November. Sion beat Lausanne narrowly on Sunday; Lausanne are bottom.", "why": "six points with 22 games left is not decisive, but Lugano are unbeaten and Basel have not won in their last three league games.", "thread_id": "2026-10-26-sports-lugano-lead-basel-stall-at-0-0", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-26", "event_date": "2026-10-25", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["FC Lugano", "FC Basel", "Grasshopper Club Zurich"]}
{"id": "2026-10-26-sports-swiss-fa-admits-fernandes-red-card-was-wrong", "date": "2026-10-26", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Swiss FA admits Fernandes red card was wrong", "summary": "The SFV says Edimilson Fernandes should only have been booked in YB's 2-0 win over St. Gallen.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/sport/fussball/super-league/statement-vom-sfv-verband-raeumt-ein-gelb-gegen-fernandes-waere-korrekt-gewesen", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "The Swiss Football Association's refereeing department says a yellow card, not a red, was the correct call for Edimilson Fernandes' challenge in Young Boys' 2-0 win over St. Gallen, even though referee Lukas Fähndrich reviewed it on video after VAR (video assistant referee) intervened. Even the fouled St. Gallen player, Görtler, called a yellow acceptable. What happens to the ban is open: under the Swiss Football League's precedent a second direct red this season means four matches, as for Thun's Marco Bürki, though Sion's Fodé Sylla got only two. [Single-source: SRF reporting the SFV's wording.]", "why": "an admitted error does not automatically undo a suspension, and with YB second the length of Fernandes' ban will decide how much it hurts.", "thread_id": "2026-10-26-sports-swiss-fa-admits-fernandes-red-card-was-wrong", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-26", "event_date": "2026-10-25", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Edimilson Fernandes", "BSC Young Boys", "Swiss Football Association"]}
{"id": "2026-10-26-sports-real-win-the-clasico-at-camp-nou", "date": "2026-10-26", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Real win the Clasico at Camp Nou", "summary": "Real Madrid beat Barcelona 2-1 at Camp Nou, cutting the La Liga gap to three points.", "url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/articles/cr3wvz20pglqo", "source_domain": "bbc.co.uk", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Kylian Mbappé scored twice, the second a late winner, in a 2-1 Real Madrid win at the Camp Nou (Barcelona's home ground). The result ended Barcelona's nine-game unbeaten domestic run and cut their league lead from a potential nine points to three. Jose Mourinho, back in charge of Real Madrid, is now six Clásicos unbeaten (four wins, two draws) in his second spell; Barcelona coach Hansi Flick said his side \"lacked freshness\". [Single-source: BBC; the official La Liga page was not reached.]", "why": "the title race in Spain is live again, with Real five wins in a row in all competitions.", "thread_id": "2026-10-26-sports-real-win-the-clasico-at-camp-nou", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-26", "event_date": "2026-10-25", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Real Madrid", "FC Barcelona", "Kylian Mbappe", "Jose Mourinho"]}
{"id": "2026-10-26-sports-carrick-close-to-exit-after-bournemouth-loss", "date": "2026-10-26", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Carrick close to exit after Bournemouth loss", "summary": "Man Utd lost 3-0 at home to Bournemouth, an eighth game without a win.", "url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/articles/cwm24jk9743yo", "source_domain": "bbc.co.uk", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "United are winless in eight matches in all competitions, the club's worst run since 2015-16, after the home defeat following a 4-1 loss at Como in the same week. Manager Michael Carrick, who would not say whether he will take the trip to Chelsea next Saturday, 31 October, said \"the responsibility is mine\". BBC's United reporter says the club's owners are in \"serious talks\" about his future — and that fans' booing at the players, not him, suggests that replacing the manager will not fix what supporters see as deeper problems. [Single-source: BBC; reports of replacement candidates are gossip and not reported here.]", "why": "a dismissal would be United's third managerial change in three seasons.", "thread_id": "2026-10-26-sports-carrick-close-to-exit-after-bournemouth-loss", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-26", "event_date": "2026-10-25", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Manchester United", "Michael Carrick", "AFC Bournemouth"]}
{"id": "2026-10-26-sports-marquez-leads-after-martin-s-crash", "date": "2026-10-26", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Marquez leads after Martin's crash", "summary": "Jorge Martin broke his forearm in the Phillip Island sprint and the Australian GP was cancelled, leaving Marquez ahead.", "url": "https://www.autosport.com/motogp/news/motogps-australian-gp-cancelled-bad-weather/10868120/", "source_domain": "autosport.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Marc Marquez (Ducati) won Saturday's sprint (a short half-distance race) as his title rival Jorge Martin crashed out of second, which gave Marquez a 10-point championship lead (Autosport, 24 Oct). Aprilia said Martin fractured his forearm radius with a suspected ulna fracture and was ruled out of Sunday (Autosport, 24 Oct). The Sunday race, the last ever at Phillip Island on the schedule, was then cancelled because low visibility grounded the medical helicopter MotoGP rules require; riders did a farewell lap behind a safety car. Autosport's reports did not say how points would be handled for the cancelled race.", "why": "Martin's injury hands Marquez a clear edge with the Qatar round (riders have asked for safety guarantees) still to come, though the remaining calendar was not confirmed in these reports.", "thread_id": "2026-10-26-sports-marquez-leads-after-martin-s-crash", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-26", "event_date": "2026-10-25", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Marc Marquez", "Jorge Martin", "MotoGP", "Aprilia"]}
{"id": "2026-10-26-sports-josi-three-assists-as-swiss-nhlers-shine", "date": "2026-10-26", "stream": "sports", "headline": "Josi three assists as Swiss NHLers shine", "summary": "Roman Josi had three assists, Lian Bichsel his first point of the season and Akira Schmid won in goal.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/sport/eishockey/nhl/nhl-in-der-nacht-auf-montag-3-facher-josi-gegen-avalanche-bichsel-mit-premiere", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["sports"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Roman Josi, captain of the Nashville Predators, had three assists in a 6-2 win over Colorado, his first three-point game since last February; he has 11 assists in 11 games, eighth in the league. Dallas's Lian Bichsel, 22, got his first point of the season in a 6-3 win over the Islanders with a plus-4 rating, and Florida's Akira Schmid made 19 saves in a 3-2 win at Chicago.", "why": "a quiet but notable night for the Swiss contingent in the NHL.", "thread_id": "2026-10-26-sports-josi-three-assists-as-swiss-nhlers-shine", "first_seen_date": "2026-10-26", "event_date": "2026-10-25", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Roman Josi", "Lian Bichsel", "Akira Schmid", "NHL"]}
